MBX-ST-04 suspended and scheduled -> schedule=true open scheduled=true suspendCount=1 raw=6 canBe(f,f)=false canBe(f,sys)=true | resume=true open scheduled=true suspendCount=0 raw=2
MBX-ST-05 open to closed -> before open scheduled=true suspendCount=2 raw=10 | close1=true closed scheduled=false suspendCount=0 raw=1 close2=false closed scheduled=false suspendCount=0 raw=1
MBX-ST-06 closed ignores resume and suspend -> resume=false suspend=false closed scheduled=false suspendCount=0 raw=1
MBX-ST-07 closed refuses scheduling -> schedule=false idle=true closed scheduled=false suspendCount=0 raw=1 canBe=false
MBX-ST-08 canBeScheduledForExecution matrix -> open: FTTT withSystemMessage=true; scheduled: FTTT withSystemMessage=true; suspended: FTFT withSystemMessage=true; suspended+scheduled: FTFT withSystemMessage=true; closed: FFFF withSystemMessage=false;
MBX-MQ-01 default queue is FIFO and counts -> new: n=0 has=false | enqueue n=1 has=true n=2 has=true n=3 has=true | dequeue [a, b, c] then null | after n=0 has=false
MBX-MQ-02 default queue stays FIFO when enqueue and dequeue interleave -> first=a rest=[b, c]
MBX-MQ-03 cleanUp moves everything to the dead-letters queue in order -> source n=0 has=false | target n=3 has=true order [a, b, c]
MBX-SQ-01 system queue drains earliest first -> has=true drain=[Suspend, Resume, Terminate] | after has=false drain=[]
MBX-SQ-02 sentinel NoMessage closes the system queue -> drain=[Suspend] | afterSentinel has=false drain=[] (actor==null: dropped, not forwarded)
MBX-TK-01 Mailbox is a plain Runnable, not a ForkJoinTask -> forkJoinTask=false runnable=true
MBX-OR-01 user messages are FIFO -> [r:1, r:2, r:3, r:4, r:5, r:6, r:7, r:8]
MBX-OR-02 system message queued behind user messages runs before them, drained after the turn's message -> inTurn: open scheduled=true suspendCount=0 queued=0 | queued: open scheduled=true suspendCount=0 queued=2 | afterTurn: open scheduled=false suspendCount=1 queued=2 log=[r:block] | afterResume: open scheduled=false suspendCount=0 queued=0 log=[r:block, r:u2, r:u3]
MBX-OR-03 suspension keeps user messages pending; nested suspend needs balanced resume -> suspended: open scheduled=false suspendCount=2 queued=2 log=[] | oneResume: open scheduled=false suspendCount=1 queued=2 log=[] | twoResumes: open scheduled=false suspendCount=0 queued=0 log=[r:u1, r:u2]
MBX-OR-04 messages sent while terminating and after termination go to dead letters -> received=[r:block] deadLetters=[u2, u3, u4, after] oldMailbox=closed scheduled=false suspendCount=0 queued=0
MBX-OR-05 system messages after close go to dead letters (Watch is answered) -> deadLetters=[Suspend, Resume] watcherLog=[terminated]
MBX-DL-01 watching deadLetters is not answered, watching a stopped actor is -> watcherLog=[terminated]
MBX-RJ-01 one rejection of the executor is retried once and the message is delivered -> log=[r:m] errors=[] rejectionsLeft=0 open scheduled=false suspendCount=0 queued=0
MBX-RJ-02 two rejections: Error published, mailbox idle, message kept and delivered by the next send -> errors=[org.apache.pekko.dispatch.Dispatcher|java.util.concurrent.RejectedExecutionException|registerForExecution was rejected twice!, pekko://mbx/user/w|java.util.concurrent.RejectedExecutionException|swallowing exception during message send] open scheduled=false suspendCount=0 queued=1 log=[] rejectionsLeft=0 | next send: log=[r:m, r:n] errors=2 open scheduled=false suspendCount=0 queued=0
MBX-RJ-03 a system message whose scheduling is rejected twice stays queued and runs with the next send -> errors=[org.apache.pekko.dispatch.Dispatcher|java.util.concurrent.RejectedExecutionException|registerForExecution was rejected twice!, pekko://mbx/user/w|java.util.concurrent.RejectedExecutionException|swallowing exception during message send] open scheduled=false suspendCount=0 queued=0 systemPending=true | next send: open scheduled=false suspendCount=1 queued=1 systemPending=false log=[]
MBX-RJ-04 a Terminate whose scheduling is rejected twice terminates the actor with the next send; the message is dead-lettered -> errors=[org.apache.pekko.dispatch.Dispatcher|java.util.concurrent.RejectedExecutionException|registerForExecution was rejected twice!, pekko://mbx/user/w|java.util.concurrent.RejectedExecutionException|swallowing exception during message send] terminated=false systemPending=true | next send: terminated=true deadLetters=[m] log=[]
MBX-RJ-05 an actor whose attach is rejected twice: actorOf returns, the supervisor fails and its children stop, the new actor never starts -> errors=[org.apache.pekko.dispatch.Dispatcher|java.util.concurrent.RejectedExecutionException|registerForExecution was rejected twice!] refReturned=true newActorTerminated=false siblingTerminated=true startedActors=1 rejectionsLeft=0
MBX-RJ-06 a synchronous context.actorOf whose attach is rejected twice: the caller gets the exception and the name stays taken -> thrown=java.util.concurrent.RejectedExecutionException errors=[org.apache.pekko.dispatch.Dispatcher|java.util.concurrent.RejectedExecutionException|registerForExecution was rejected twice!] rejectionsLeft=0 | again=org.apache.pekko.actor.InvalidActorNameException startedActors=1 parentTerminated=false
MBX-RJ-07 a synchronous context.actorOf whose attach is rejected twice and whose exception escapes: the parent fails and restarts -> again=ok dispatcherErrors=[org.apache.pekko.dispatch.Dispatcher|java.util.concurrent.RejectedExecutionException|registerForExecution was rejected twice!] rejectionsLeft=0 startedActors=2 parentTerminated=false
MBX-PT-01 a send that waits for the unstarted cell's lock longer than unstarted-push-timeout is a dead letter with a Warning -> waitedTheTimeout=true returnedWithinBound=true deadLetters=[m2] warnings=[pekko://mbx/user/spawner/c|org.apache.pekko.actor.UnstartedCell|dropping message of typeclass java.lang.String due to lock timeout] log=[r:m1]
MBX-PT-02 a send that waits for the lock while the hand-over ends before the timeout is delivered after the queued messages -> log=[r:m1, r:m2] deadLetters=[] warnings=[]
MBX-PT-03 a system message waits for the lock without a timeout and is delivered once the hand-over ends -> stillBlockedAfterThreeTimeouts=true suspendCount=1 deadLetters=[] warnings=[]
MBX-PT-06 the thread that hands the queue over can send to the same reference: its message joins the queue, not the timeout -> log=[r:m1, r:m2] deadLetters=[] warnings=[]
MBX-PT-04 unstarted-push-timeout = 0s: a send that finds the lock held is dropped at once -> returnedWithinBound=true deadLetters=[m2] warnings=[pekko://mbx/user/spawner/c|org.apache.pekko.actor.UnstartedCell|dropping message of typeclass java.lang.String due to lock timeout] log=[r:m1]
MBX-PT-05 unstarted-push-timeout = -1s: a send that finds the lock held is dropped at once -> returnedWithinBound=true deadLetters=[m2] warnings=[pekko://mbx/user/spawner/c|org.apache.pekko.actor.UnstartedCell|dropping message of typeclass java.lang.String due to lock timeout] log=[r:m1]
MBX-UC-01 messages sent to an unstarted actor: the system message goes first, then the user messages in order -> afterStart: open scheduled=false suspendCount=1 queued=2 log=[] | afterResume: open scheduled=false suspendCount=0 queued=0 log=[r:m1, r:m2]
MBX-UC-02 a Watch and a Terminate sent to an unstarted actor are applied once it starts: the watcher gets Terminated -> watcherLog=[terminated] childTerminated=true
MBX-UC-03 a Watch undone by an Unwatch before the actor starts: the watcher is not told -> watcherLog=[] childTerminated=true
MBX-UC-04 a child created under a suspended parent inherits the suspension -> childUnderSuspendedParent: open scheduled=false suspendCount=1 queued=1 log=[] | afterResume: open scheduled=false suspendCount=0 queued=0 log=[r:u]
MBX-IF-01 the cell of an asynchronously created actor cannot be made: actorOf returns, the supervisor stops the actor, which never starts -> refReturned=true started=0 terminated=true nameReusable=created
MBX-IF-02 messages sent to an actor whose cell cannot be made, before and after it is stopped, are dead letters -> dead=[after, before] log=[] started=0
MBX-IF-03 a supervisor that restarts on ActorInitializationException: the failed creation becomes a Create and the actor starts -> errors=[pekko://mbx/user/parent/c|org.apache.pekko.event.Logging$Error$NoCause$|changing Recreate into Create after org.apache.pekko.actor.ActorInitializationException: pekko://mbx/user/parent/c: failure while creating ActorCell] started=1 log=[r:m] terminated=false
MBX-IF-04 an actor that fails to start after creating a child is restarted as a Create: its children are stopped first -> errors=[pekko://mbx/user/sup/c|org.apache.pekko.event.Logging$Error$NoCause$|changing Recreate into Create after org.apache.pekko.actor.ActorInitializationException: pekko://mbx/user/sup/c: exception during creation, root cause message: [first start fails]] starts=2 childStarts=2 log=[preStart:1, preStart:2, r:m] terminated=false
MBX-IF-05 a supervisor that resumes on ActorInitializationException: the failed creation becomes a Create and the actor starts -> errors=[pekko://mbx/user/parent/c|org.apache.pekko.event.Logging$Error$NoCause$|changing Resume into Create after org.apache.pekko.actor.ActorInitializationException: pekko://mbx/user/parent/c: failure while creating ActorCell] started=1 log=[r:m] terminated=false
